> I solved it.  The auto.th <http://auto.th> parameter was the key, defaulting to TRUE in
> cfa() but FALSE in lavaan().
>
> Perhaps at some point in the future an internal check for the ordered
> parameter could be added to provide a more informative error than the
> current "non-conformable arguments" error.

Agreed. I changed this in dev 0.5-18.757. If we have ordered variables,
thresholds will now always be included in the parameter table. Not as
free parameters (this would still require auto.th <http://auto.th> = TRUE), but as fixed
parameters (ie the thresholds are fixed to their sample-based values).

A similar change related to intercepts and variances took place in 0.5-17.

(Note: this is only relevant for users of the lavaan() function.)

Yves.

