Hi,

I have a simple SEM model:

model <- '
   # latent variables
     L1 =~ x1 + x2 + x3
     L2 =~ x4 + x5 + x6

   # regression
     L1 ~ L2
'

So far so good. Now I would like to estimate the parameter for a quadratic relationship; Explicitly, I would like to have this regression:

L1 ~ poly(L2,2)

#or

L1 ~ L2 + I(L2^2)

However, this syntax does not work in lavaan. How I can do that using the lavaan syntax?

My workaround would be to square the indicator variabales x4, x5, x6, but that seems a bit inelegant and I am also not completely sure whether this is equivalent.

Any help is appreciated!

Thanks,
Jonas

