Hi Yves,

In semTools::moreFitIndices(), we use a hidden function semTools:::sic() to calculate the stochastic information criterion (SIC).  The calculation requires the the determinant of the information matrix, which we retrieve using

> solve(vcov(fit))

I just tried this for the first time on a model with equality constraints for factor loadings, and it returns an error because the vcov(fit) has redundant parameter estimates along the diagonal that are perfectly correlated (e.g., visual=~x1 is perfectly correlated with visual=~x1.g2, etc.).  Here is a working example:

> mod.metric <- '
> visual  =~ x1 + x2 + x3
> textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
> speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9
> visual ~~ c(1, NA)*visual
> textual ~~ c(1, NA)*textual
> speed ~~ c(1, NA)*speed
